<!-- Seat fee, who pays, who is at the table. -->
<section class="facts">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Before you sign up</p>
      <h2>The plain version</h2>
    </div>
    <dl>
      <dt>The seat</dt>
      <dd>
        $25 per person, charged when you accept an invitation to a specific
        table.
      </dd>

      <dt>Food and drinks</dt>
      <dd>
        Ordered and paid at each stop, the way you would any other night out.
        Your seat fee covers the arrangement, not the check.
      </dd>

      <dt>Who's at the table</dt>
      <dd>
        Five single adults, 21 and over, each one identity-verified before
        they're seated. No profiles to swipe and no photos of your table
        beforehand.
      </dd>

      <dt>How often</dt>
      <dd>
        One night. There's no subscription and no obligation to come back,
        though most tables run Thursday through Saturday evenings.
      </dd>

      <dt>If it's a no</dt>
      <dd>
        You had dinner in a good restaurant with four interesting people. That's
        the floor, and the floor is fine.
      </dd>
    </dl>
  </div>
</section>
